  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ExtensionObject_decodeBinaryContent",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_types_encoding_binary.c",
    "description": "In the unknown-type path, `dst->content.encoded.typeId = *typeId` performs a shallow copy of a NodeId that may own a dynamically allocated string/ByteString identifier. After this helper returns, `ExtensionObject_decodeBinary` unconditionally calls `UA_NodeId_deleteMembers(&binTypeId)`, freeing that identifier while the decoded ExtensionObject still points to it. A later `UA_copy` reaches `ExtensionObject_copy`/`NodeId_copy` and reads the freed identifier in `UA_Array_copy`/`memcpy`, causing the heap-use-after-free. The unknown-type branch must move ownership without subsequently freeing the source, or deep-copy the NodeId and handle copy failure.",
    "conditions": "The fuzz input selects a type containing ExtensionObjects and supplies a binary ExtensionObject whose type NodeId is not found by `UA_findDataTypeByBinaryInternal`, whose NodeId identifier is a heap-owning string or ByteString, and whose encoded body is otherwise valid so decoding returns `UA_STATUSCODE_GOOD`. The harness then calls `UA_copy` on the decoded object; the retained encoded typeId references memory freed when the temporary `binTypeId` was destroyed at line 947, triggering the UAF during NodeId string copying."
  },
